**How to implement.** The constructor windows compose the wizard, and the section is proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder (the S9.2 brief; .spec-md §3.13: AT-2 writes its observation files through the Mueller-matrix profile; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (steps 189, 233): the shell it builds is followed by `.withImportWizard window dispatch` (step 311), over the dispatch it captures from its init command, and the file opens `OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardOpening`, so a constructor window's Attach data file… opens the real wizard over itself. Its doc says so in no more words; nothing else in it changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 297) gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: Attach data file maps a picked lab file through the wizard into the kit and validates it`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write through `openKitAt`, holding experiment `E1` (a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360°, as step 310's facts record it) and loaded into `initInverse`, the fact keeps the model and dispatches through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell being `KitWindowShell.inert.withImportWizard <a shown headless host Window> <that dispatch>`, as `mount` composes it. `OpenImportWizard (ExperimentId 1, <a Phone ROI file written outside the kit as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\n`>)` shows a window carrying `importWizardWindow`; pressing `importWizardProfileChoice` of `Phone ROI CSV` and then `importWizardAttachButton` at their centres closes it and leaves E1's `dataOpt` an attachment at `data/<the file's leaf>` mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` over every row, the kit folder holding that file with exactly the picked bytes, E1's file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same mapped attachment, and `model.dataBadgeOf E1`'s text `validated (2 points)`. (3) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'An experiment is a scan over a setup revision' (step 297), one bullet of at most six lines: **Lab files are read through import profiles** (`ImportProfiles.fs`, `LabFileImport.fs`, spec 0050 S9.2): an experiment's data is a kit file, a profile name and a row selection; a profile is a built-in (`Intensity series`, `Ellipsometric series`, `Phone ROI CSV`, `Mueller-matrix observations`, each calling its parser) or a named column mapping in `.kit-json`, never replaced once saved; `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` is the one read and `MappedPoints.validatedFor` the one validation; the app writes only observation files (`KeyedObservation.observationFileText`); Attach data file… opens the wizard, whose Attach sends `SaveImportProfile` then `AttachDataFile`. Nothing else in the file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the wizard is wired, the constructor windows' shell MUST open the real wizard over the window's dispatch, a picked lab file MUST be mapped through the wizard into the kit, attached and validated end to end, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Attach data file maps a picked lab file through the wizard into the kit and validates it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
